1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Your dot. In iMessage.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,500
A familiar conversation.
An active agent behind it.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:10,000
iPhone → Photon Spectrum → existing runtime

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Keep the transport.
Connect it to the active task.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Save it before you process it.
Persist. Batch. Claim.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
A saved batch. A single owner.
An expiring claim.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The active dot task reads the batch
and authors the reply.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
No separate model in the listener.
No automatic platform wake.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Outbox → Photon → the same iMessage thread

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Queued, provider accepted, and read receipt
are distinct states.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The local Moonshine pipeline
turns audio into text.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Local audio path verified.
Phone-to-dot voice check still pending.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Initial text test: inbound, reply, read receipt.
Local audio conversion and transcription verified.

14
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,000
Full phone checks are still required.
Needs a running bridge and active dot task.

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
iMessage is the interface.
dot stays the agent.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Photon carries the messages.
dot authors the response.
